clause!(s31_1_c_r1, "31.1", "Contract", r##"| `ldconfig` | `/usr/sbin/ldconfig` | a shell script wrapper over a static program (Liella: one program, §31.2) | probe `paths`, `ldconfig-help` |"##);
clause!(s31_1_c_r2, "31.1", "Contract", r##"| `ldd` | `/usr/bin/ldd` | a shell script | probe `paths` |"##);
clause!(s31_1_c_r3, "31.1", "Contract", r##"| `getent`, `getconf`, `iconv`, `locale`, `localedef`, `zdump`, `gencat`, `pldd` | `/usr/bin/<name>` | dynamic programs | probe `paths` |"##);
clause!(s31_1_c_r4, "31.1", "Contract", r##"| `zic` | `/usr/sbin/zic` | a dynamic program | probe `paths` |"##);
clause!(s31_1_c_r5, "31.1", "Contract", r##"| `tzselect` | `/usr/bin/tzselect` | a shell script | probe `paths` |"##);
clause!(s31_1_c_r6, "31.1", "Contract", r##"| `ld.so` | `/usr/bin/ld.so` | a symbolic link to `../lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2` | probe `ldso-link` |"##);
clause!(s31_1_c_1, "31.1", "Contract", r##"The paths are part of the interface: scripts name them (`/sbin/ldconfig` reaches `/usr/sbin/ldconfig` on a merged-`/usr` system), and `dpkg` refuses to configure any package when `ldconfig` is not in `PATH`: `dpkg: warning: 'ldconfig' not found in PATH or not executable`, then `dpkg: error: 2 expected programs not found in PATH or not executable`, exit 2 (probe `dpkg-needs-ldconfig`). ⚑ COMPAT."##);
clause!(s31_1_c_2, "31.1", "Contract", r##"The argp-style commands (`ldconfig`, `getent`, `iconv`, `locale`, `localedef`, `gencat`, `pldd`) accept `-?`/`--help`, `--usage` and `-V`/`--version`; `ldd`, `zic`, `zdump` and `tzselect` accept `--help` and `--version`; `getconf` accepts `--help` and `--version` (probe `*-help`, `*-version`)."##);
clause!(s31_1_g_1, "31.1", "Guarantees", r##"`--help` writes the usage text to standard output and exits 0 (probe `*-help`, every case `rc=0`)."##);
clause!(s31_1_g_2, "31.1", "Guarantees", r##"`--version` writes a banner whose first line is `<command> (<identity>) 2.39` and exits 0 (probe `*-version`: `ldd (Ubuntu GLIBC 2.39-0ubuntu8.9) 2.39`). **Liella rule:** `<identity>` is `Liella <version>`, and the bug-report line of `--help` names Liella's channel (pending `UTIL-SPEC-4`; differences row "Identity strings of the utilities")."##);
clause!(s31_1_f_1, "31.1", "Failure", r##"An argp-style usage error writes the message and ``Try `<command> --help' or `<command> --usage' for more information.`` (probe `getent-unknowndb`, `iconv-unsupported`, `pldd-nopid`); the exit status is the command's (§31.2-§31.13)."##);
clause!(s31_2_c_1, "31.2", "Contract", r##"Builds the loader cache (Appendix D.3) from the directories of the configuration and the trusted directories, and creates or updates the soname links in them (ldconfig(8))."##);
clause!(s31_2_c_2, "31.2", "Contract", r##"`dpkg` runs it through the `ldconfig` trigger (`activate-noawait ldconfig` in a package's `triggers` file) after library packages change; Liella's `libc-bin` declares interest in that trigger (pending `UTIL-SPEC-2`)."##);
clause!(s31_2_i_1, "31.2", "Inputs", r##"Options (probe `ldconfig-help`): `-c`/`--format=FORMAT`, `-C CACHE`, `-f CONF`, `-i`/`--ignore-aux-cache`, `-l`, `-n`, `-N`, `-p`/`--print-cache`, `-r ROOT`, `-v`/`--verbose`, `-X`, `-?`/`--help`, `--usage`, `-V`/`--version`; operands are directories (with `-n`, only those) or, with `-l`, library files (ldconfig(8))."##);
clause!(s31_2_i_2, "31.2", "Inputs", r##"`/etc/ld.so.conf` (default; `-f CONF` replaces it): one directory per line, `#` comments, `include <glob>` lines read in sorted order; the reference ships `include /etc/ld.so.conf.d/*.conf` (probe `ld.so.conf`; ldconfig(8))."##);
clause!(s31_2_i_3, "31.2", "Inputs", r##"The trusted directories are scanned after the configured ones: `/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu`, `/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu`, `/lib`, `/usr/lib` (the same list as the loader's default directories, D-27.16); a directory reached twice is scanned once (ldconfig(8))."##);
clause!(s31_2_i_4, "31.2", "Inputs", r##"`-r ROOT`: the configuration, the scanned directories and the cache are taken inside ROOT; the reference does this for an ordinary user too (probe `ldconfig-r-user`, exit 0). **Liella rule** (mechanism only, not observable): paths are resolved inside ROOT without `chroot` (pending `UTIL-SPEC-9`)."##);
clause!(s31_2_g_1, "31.2", "Guarantees", r##"The cache is written in the D.3.1 new format with the D.3.2 extensions (tag 0 generator text, tag 1 hwcaps names) (probe `ldconfig-c-new`: the file starts `glibc-ld.so.cache1.1`; pending `UTIL-SPEC-3`)."##);
clause!(s31_2_g_2, "31.2", "Guarantees", r##"The cache is replaced through a temporary file `<cache>~` (probe `ldconfig-user`). **Liella rule:** the temporary file is in the cache's directory, synced, then renamed over the cache, so a reader sees the old or the new file whole (pending `UTIL-SPEC-9`)."##);
clause!(s31_2_g_3, "31.2", "Guarantees", r##"**Liella rule:** the cache is deterministic: entries in the D.3.3 order, ties broken by configuration order and then path bytes, directory listings sorted, so the same tree gives byte-identical caches on any file system; every ELF file read is untrusted input, bounds-checked and never mapped executable (pending `UTIL-SPEC-9`)."##);
clause!(s31_2_g_4, "31.2", "Guarantees", r##"Soname links (probe `ldconfig-n-links`): in each scanned directory, the link `<soname>` points to the file with that `DT_SONAME` whose name has the highest version under the D.3.3 comparison (`libfoo.so.1` -> `libfoo.so.1.10` among `1.2`, `1.9`, `1.10`); a file without `DT_SONAME` is keyed by its own name and gets no link; a development link (`libfoo.so`) is left as it is; `-X` makes no links, `-N` builds no cache (ldconfig(8))."##);
clause!(s31_2_g_5, "31.2", "Guarantees", r##"`-v` prints `<dir>: (from <file>:<line>)` per directory (`<cmdline>:0` for an operand) and `\t<soname> -> <file>` per library, with ` (changed)` when the link was created or changed (probe `ldconfig-n-links`)."##);
clause!(s31_2_g_6, "31.2", "Guarantees", r##"`-p` prints ``<N> libs found in cache `<cache>'``, then `\t<key> (<flags>) => <path>` per entry in cache order (`(libc6,x86-64)` for this architecture), then `Cache generated by: <tag 0 text>` (probe `ldconfig-p`); callers parse it (CPython's `ctypes.util.find_library` matches `(libc6,x86-64`). ⚑ COMPAT."##);
clause!(s31_2_f_1, "31.2", "Failure", r##"A cache that cannot be opened by `-p`: `<program>: Can't open cache file <cache>` and the strerror text on the next line, exit 1 (probe `ldconfig-p-missing`)."##);
clause!(s31_2_f_2, "31.2", "Failure", r##"A cache directory that is not writable: `<program>: Can't create temporary cache file <cache>~: Permission denied`, exit 1 (probe `ldconfig-user`)."##);
clause!(s31_2_f_3, "31.2", "Failure", r##"`-c old` and `-c compat`: the reference writes the old format (probe `ldconfig-c-old`: the file starts `ld.so-1.7.0`). **Liella rule:** refused with a message and a nonzero exit, nothing written; `-c new` is accepted (pending `UTIL-SPEC-6`; differences row "`ldconfig -c old`, `-c compat`")."##);
clause!(s31_3_c_1, "31.3", "Contract", r##"Prints the shared objects each operand needs, as the loader would resolve them; the same list as `LD_TRACE_LOADED_OBJECTS=1` or the loader's `--list` (ld.so(8), ldd(1); D-27.16)."##);
clause!(s31_3_c_2, "31.3", "Contract", r##"**Liella rule:** ldd never runs the operand's code or an interpreter other than Liella's loader: it lists through Liella's loader in list mode, and for an operand whose `PT_INTERP` names another loader it lists by Liella's rules and says so on standard error (pending `UTIL-SPEC-7`; differences row "`ldd` on a program for another loader")."##);
clause!(s31_3_i_1, "31.3", "Inputs", r##"`ldd [OPTION]... FILE...`; options `--help`, `--version`, `-d`/`--data-relocs`, `-r`/`--function-relocs`, `-u`/`--unused`, `-v`/`--verbose` (probe `ldd-help`). **Liella rule:** `-d`, `-r` and `-u` are refused with a message until the loader processes relocations of a listed program (DL-10; pending `UTIL-SPEC-7`)."##);
clause!(s31_3_g_1, "31.3", "Guarantees", r##"One line per object, each starting with a TAB: `\tlinux-vdso.so.1 (0x<16 hex digits>)`, `\t<name> => <path> (0x<16 hex digits>)`, and the program's interpreter `\t/lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2 (0x<16 hex digits>)`, exit 0 (probe `ldd-dynamic`); a dependency not found is `\t<name> => not found` (D-27.16). initramfs-tools parses these lines (the TAB, the path after `=>`, the word before ` (`). ⚑ COMPAT."##);
clause!(s31_3_g_2, "31.3", "Guarantees", r##"With several operands, a `<file>:` line before each list (probe `ldd-two`)."##);
clause!(s31_3_g_3, "31.3", "Guarantees", r##"`-v` adds a blank line, `\tVersion information:`, and per object `\t<object>:` followed by `\t\t<needed> (<version>) => <path>` per version need (probe `ldd-v`)."##);
clause!(s31_3_g_4, "31.3", "Guarantees", r##"A static-pie program: `\tstatically linked` on standard output, exit 0 (probe `ldd-static-pie`)."##);
clause!(s31_3_f_1, "31.3", "Failure", r##"A file that is not a dynamic ELF program, including a static program that is not position independent: `\tnot a dynamic executable` on standard error, exit 1 (probe `ldd-notelf`, `ldd-static`)."##);
clause!(s31_3_f_2, "31.3", "Failure", r##"A missing operand file: `ldd: <file>: No such file or directory`, exit 1 (probe `ldd-missing`)."##);
clause!(s31_3_f_3, "31.3", "Failure", r##"No operand: `ldd: missing file arguments` and ``Try `ldd --help' for more information.``, exit 1 (probe `ldd-none`)."##);
clause!(s31_4_c_1, "31.4", "Contract", r##"Prints entries of the name-service databases through the library's own functions (§16, §17), so it shows what every program gets from `nsswitch.conf` and its modules (getent(1))."##);
clause!(s31_4_i_1, "31.4", "Inputs", r##"`getent [OPTION...] database [key ...]`; options `-A`/`--no-addrconfig`, `-i`/`--no-idn`, `-s`/`--service=CONFIG`, `-?`/`--help`, `--usage`, `-V`/`--version`; databases `ahosts ahostsv4 ahostsv6 aliases ethers group gshadow hosts initgroups netgroup networks passwd protocols rpc services shadow` (probe `getent-help`)."##);
clause!(s31_4_i_2, "31.4", "Inputs", r##"`-s files` selects the service for the lookup (probe `getent-s`; getent(1))."##);
clause!(s31_4_g_1, "31.4", "Guarantees", r##"`passwd`, `group` and the other file databases print the entry in its file's line form (`root:x:0:0:root:/root:/bin/bash`; probe `getent-passwd`, `getent-group`)."##);
clause!(s31_4_g_2, "31.4", "Guarantees", r##"`hosts`: the address left-justified in 15 columns, a space, the names (probe `getent-hosts`); `ahosts`: per address the lines `<address padded> STREAM <canonical name>`, `<address padded> DGRAM`, `<address padded> RAW` (probe `getent-ahosts`); `services`: the name left-justified in 21 columns, a space, `<port>/<protocol>` (probe `getent-services`); `initgroups`: the user left-justified in 21 columns, a space, the group ids (probe `getent-initgroups`)."##);
clause!(s31_4_g_3, "31.4", "Guarantees", r##"Without a key, the database is enumerated, exit 0 (getent(1))."##);
clause!(s31_4_f_1, "31.4", "Failure", r##"A key not found: no output, exit 2 (probe `getent-notfound`)."##);
clause!(s31_4_f_2, "31.4", "Failure", r##"An unknown database: `Unknown database: <db>` and the `Try` line, exit 1 (probe `getent-unknowndb`)."##);
clause!(s31_4_f_3, "31.4", "Failure", r##"Enumeration of a database that cannot be enumerated: `Enumeration not supported on <db>`, exit 3 (probe `getent-noenum`)."##);
clause!(s31_5_c_1, "31.5", "Contract", r##"Prints configuration values from `sysconf`, `confstr` and `pathconf` (§24) by name (POSIX `getconf`)."##);
clause!(s31_5_i_1, "31.5", "Inputs", r##"`getconf [-v SPEC] NAME`, `getconf [-v SPEC] PATH_NAME PATH`, `getconf -a [PATH]`, `--help`, `--version` (POSIX `getconf`; probe `getconf-help`, `getconf-pathvar-nopath`)."##);
clause!(s31_5_i_2, "31.5", "Inputs", r##"Names: the POSIX set, plus `GNU_LIBC_VERSION`, `GNU_LIBPTHREAD_VERSION`, `PAGESIZE`, `PAGE_SIZE`, `_NPROCESSORS_ONLN`, `LONG_BIT`, `PATH`, `LFS_CFLAGS`, `POSIX_V7_LP64_OFF64_CFLAGS` and the others `getconf -a` lists (320 lines on the reference; probe `getconf-a`). Scripts use `_NPROCESSORS_ONLN` and `PAGESIZE`. ⚑ COMPAT."##);
clause!(s31_5_g_1, "31.5", "Guarantees", r##"A value on one line: `PAGESIZE` `4096`, `LONG_BIT` `64`, `PATH` `/bin:/usr/bin`, `GNU_LIBC_VERSION` `glibc 2.39`, `GNU_LIBPTHREAD_VERSION` `NPTL 2.39`, `LFS_CFLAGS` empty, `POSIX_V7_LP64_OFF64_CFLAGS` `-m64`, exit 0 (probe `getconf-values`); `_NPROCESSORS_ONLN` a positive integer (probe `getconf-nproc`); `NAME_MAX /` `255` (probe `getconf-pathvar`). The `GNU_LIBC_VERSION` value is `confstr`'s (§24), not a getconf decision."##);
clause!(s31_5_g_2, "31.5", "Guarantees", r##"`-a` prints each name left-justified and padded, then its value (probe `getconf-a`: values start in column 36 for `LONG_BIT`, `PAGESIZE`, `GNU_LIBC_VERSION`)."##);
clause!(s31_5_g_3, "31.5", "Guarantees", r##"`-v` with a specification accepts any name, known or not, and prints the value (probe `getconf-v`)."##);
clause!(s31_5_f_1, "31.5", "Failure", r##"An unknown name: ``getconf: Unrecognized variable `<NAME>'``, exit 2 (probe `getconf-unknown`)."##);
clause!(s31_5_f_2, "31.5", "Failure", r##"A path variable without a path: the usage text on standard error, exit 2 (probe `getconf-pathvar-nopath`)."##);
clause!(s31_6_c_1, "31.6", "Contract", r##"Converts text between character sets through `iconv(3)` (§6), as any program would (POSIX `iconv`)."##);
clause!(s31_6_i_1, "31.6", "Inputs", r##"`iconv [OPTION...] [FILE...]`; options `-f`/`--from-code=NAME`, `-t`/`--to-code=NAME` (with `//TRANSLIT` and `//IGNORE`), `-l`/`--list`, `-c`, `-o`/`--output=FILE`, `-s`/`--silent`, `--verbose`, `-?`/`--help`, `--usage`, `-V`/`--version` (probe `iconv-help`); no FILE or `-` reads standard input (POSIX `iconv`)."##);
clause!(s31_6_i_2, "31.6", "Inputs", r##"The character sets are the library's (§6): Liella's built-ins and the charmaps of `/usr/share/i18n/charmaps` (D-6.8)."##);
clause!(s31_6_g_1, "31.6", "Guarantees", r##"The converted bytes on standard output or in the `-o` file (probe `iconv-o`)."##);
clause!(s31_6_g_2, "31.6", "Guarantees", r##"`-c` omits characters that cannot be converted, exit 0 (probe `iconv-c`); `//TRANSLIT` replaces them by the target set's transliteration or `?` (probe `iconv-translit`)."##);
clause!(s31_6_g_3, "31.6", "Guarantees", r##"`-l` lists the names the command accepts. **Liella rule:** exactly the names it can convert (the reference lists 1180 names of its conversion modules, `437//` style; probe `iconv-l`); differences row "Character sets of `iconv` and `iconv -l`"."##);
clause!(s31_6_f_1, "31.6", "Failure", r##"Invalid input: the output up to the error is written, then `iconv: illegal input sequence at position <N>` (N the byte offset), exit 1 (probe `iconv-illegal`); the same for a character the target set cannot hold without `-c` (probe `iconv-unconvertible`); with `//IGNORE`, the remaining output is written and the message and exit 1 still follow (probe `iconv-ignore`)."##);
clause!(s31_6_f_2, "31.6", "Failure", r##"An unknown character set: ``iconv: conversion from `<NAME>' is not supported`` (or `to`) and the `Try` line, exit 1 (probe `iconv-unsupported`)."##);
clause!(s31_6_f_3, "31.6", "Failure", r##"An input file that cannot be opened: ``iconv: cannot open input file `<FILE>': <strerror>``, exit 1 (probe `iconv-nofile`)."##);
clause!(s31_7_c_1, "31.7", "Contract", r##"Reports the current locale settings, the available locales and charmaps, and the values of locale keywords (POSIX `locale`; locale(1))."##);
clause!(s31_7_i_1, "31.7", "Inputs", r##"`locale [OPTION...] NAME...` or `locale [OPTION...] [-a|-m]`; options `-a`/`--all-locales`, `-m`/`--charmaps`, `-c`/`--category-name`, `-k`/`--keyword-name`, `-v`/`--verbose`, `-?`/`--help`, `--usage`, `-V`/`--version` (probe `locale-help`)."##);
clause!(s31_7_i_2, "31.7", "Inputs", r##"The environment: `LANG`, `LANGUAGE`, `LC_ALL` and the twelve `LC_*` variables (POSIX XBD 8.2)."##);
clause!(s31_7_g_1, "31.7", "Guarantees", r##"Without operands: `LANG=<value>`, `LANGUAGE=<value>`, then each of `LC_CTYPE`, `LC_NUMERIC`, `LC_TIME`, `LC_COLLATE`, `LC_MONETARY`, `LC_MESSAGES`, `LC_PAPER`, `LC_NAME`, `LC_ADDRESS`, `LC_TELEPHONE`, `LC_MEASUREMENT`, `LC_IDENTIFICATION` as `NAME="<value>"` when derived from `LANG` or the default and `NAME=<value>` when set itself, then `LC_ALL=<value>` (probe `locale-noenv`, `locale-lang`)."##);
clause!(s31_7_g_2, "31.7", "Guarantees", r##"`-a`: `C`, `C.utf8`, `POSIX` and the installed locales with normalised codeset names (probe `locale-a`); `-a -v`: per locale `locale: <name> directory: <path>` (or `archive: <path>`), a rule line and its `LC_IDENTIFICATION` fields (`title`, `email`, `revision`, `date`, `codeset`) (probe `locale-a-v`). Liella builds `C.utf8` into the library and still lists it (`plan/utilities.md` §2.1); what `-a -v` prints for it is left to UTIL-8."##);
clause!(s31_7_g_3, "31.7", "Guarantees", r##"`-m`: the charmap names (probe `locale-m`)."##);
clause!(s31_7_g_4, "31.7", "Guarantees", r##"A keyword operand prints its value; with `-k` as `keyword=value`, strings quoted and numbers bare, including the wide-character items (`numeric-decimal-point-wc=46`); a category operand prints all its keywords; `-c` adds the category name first (probe `locale-k`, `locale-ck`, `locale-category`). `locale charmap` prints the codeset (`ANSI_X3.4-1968` in `POSIX`; probe `locale-charmap`)."##);
clause!(s31_7_f_1, "31.7", "Failure", r##"An unknown operand: `locale: unknown name "<name>"`, exit 1 (probe `locale-unknown`)."##);
clause!(s31_7_f_2, "31.7", "Failure", r##"A locale variable naming a locale that is not installed: the values are still printed, and `locale: Cannot set LC_CTYPE to default locale: No such file or directory` (also for `LC_MESSAGES` and `LC_ALL`) on standard error, exit 0 (probe `locale-missing`)."##);
clause!(s31_8_c_1, "31.8", "Contract", r##"Compiles a locale source and a charmap into the binary locale files of Appendix D.1, as a directory or into the locale archive (D.1.6) (POSIX `localedef`; localedef(1))."##);
clause!(s31_8_i_1, "31.8", "Inputs", r##"`localedef [OPTION...] NAME`, `localedef [OPTION...] --add-to-archive|--delete-from-archive FILE...`, `localedef [OPTION...] --list-archive [FILE]`; options `-f`/`--charmap`, `-i`/`--inputfile`, `-u`/`--repertoire-map`, `-c`/`--force`, `--no-hard-links`, `--no-warnings=`, `--warnings=` (`ascii`, `intcurrsym`), `--posix`, `--prefix=`, `--quiet`, `-v`/`--verbose`, `-A`/`--alias-file`, `--big-endian`, `--little-endian`, `--no-archive`, `--replace`, `-?`/`--help`, `--usage`, `-V`/`--version` (probe `localedef-help`)."##);
clause!(s31_8_i_2, "31.8", "Inputs", r##"Search paths (probe `localedef-help-paths`): charmaps `/usr/share/i18n/charmaps`, repertoire maps `/usr/share/i18n/repertoiremaps`, locale sources `/usr/lib/locale:/usr/share/i18n`."##);
clause!(s31_8_g_1, "31.8", "Guarantees", r##"A NAME containing `/` receives the directory form: `LC_ADDRESS`, `LC_COLLATE`, `LC_CTYPE`, `LC_IDENTIFICATION`, `LC_MEASUREMENT`, `LC_MESSAGES/SYS_LC_MESSAGES`, `LC_MONETARY`, `LC_NAME`, `LC_NUMERIC`, `LC_PAPER`, `LC_TELEPHONE`, `LC_TIME` (probe `localedef-dir`), in the D.1 format (pending `UTIL-SPEC-3`); otherwise the locale goes into the archive unless `--no-archive` (localedef(1))."##);
clause!(s31_8_g_2, "31.8", "Guarantees", r##"`--list-archive` prints one locale name per line (probe `localedef-list`)."##);
clause!(s31_8_f_1, "31.8", "Failure", r##"A missing source or charmap: `[error] ...` lines and exit 4, no output produced (probe `localedef-nosource`, `localedef-nocharmap`; POSIX `localedef` exit status 4: errors, no output created)."##);
clause!(s31_9_c_1, "31.9", "Contract", r##"Compiles time-zone source (the `Rule`, `Zone`, `Link`, `Leap` and `Expires` lines of zic(8)) into TZif files (RFC 8536; tzfile(5)); Liella's `localtime` reads the same files (§23.5)."##);
clause!(s31_9_i_1, "31.9", "Inputs", r##"Options (probe `zic-help`; zic(8)): `--version`, `--help`, `-v`, `-b slim|fat`, `-d DIRECTORY`, `-l LOCALTIME`, `-L LEAPSECONDS`, `-p POSIXRULES`, `-r '[@lo][/@hi]'`, `-t LINK`, then source files."##);
clause!(s31_9_i_2, "31.9", "Inputs", r##"`tzdata` installs `/usr/share/zoneinfo/tzdata.zi` (`# version 2026e` on the reference) and fat TZif version 2 files (`Europe/London` 3664 bytes); there is no `posix/` or `right/` tree (probe `zic-tzdata`)."##);
clause!(s31_9_g_1, "31.9", "Guarantees", r##"One TZif file per zone under the output directory, a link per `Link` line (probe `zic-compile`), in RFC 8536 version 2 or later (the file starts `TZif2`; pending `UTIL-SPEC-3`)."##);
clause!(s31_9_g_2, "31.9", "Guarantees", r##"`-b fat` is the default (a one-zone source gives 1256 bytes; `-b slim` 140 bytes; probe `zic-compile`, `zic-slim`)."##);
clause!(s31_9_g_3, "31.9", "Guarantees", r##"The footer TZ string reproduces the last transitions (RFC 8536 §3.3)."##);
clause!(s31_9_f_1, "31.9", "Failure", r##"A source file that cannot be opened: `zic: Can't open <file>: <strerror>`, exit 1 (probe `zic-nofile`)."##);
clause!(s31_10_c_1, "31.10", "Contract", r##"Prints the current time or the transitions of each named zone, read through the TZif files (zdump(8))."##);
clause!(s31_10_i_1, "31.10", "Inputs", r##"`zdump [OPTION]... TIMEZONE...`; options `-c [L,]U` (years, default -500 to 2500), `-t [L,]U` (seconds since 1970), `-i`, `-v`, `-V`, `--help`, `--version` (probe `zdump-help`); `TZDIR` names the zone directory (probe `zdump-test`)."##);
clause!(s31_10_g_1, "31.10", "Guarantees", r##"Plain: `<zone> <date as by ctime> <abbreviation>` (probe `zdump-plain`)."##);
clause!(s31_10_g_2, "31.10", "Guarantees", r##"`-v`: per transition two lines, the second before it and the transition itself, as `<zone> <UT date> UT = <local date> <abbr> isdst=<0|1> gmtoff=<seconds>`, framed by `<zone> -9223372036854775808 = NULL`, `-9223372036854689408 = NULL` at the start and `9223372036854689407 = NULL`, `9223372036854775807 = NULL` at the end (probe `zdump-v`, `zdump-t`); `-V` the same lines without the frame (probe `zdump-V`)."##);
clause!(s31_10_g_3, "31.10", "Guarantees", r##"`-i` (experimental in its own help): a blank line, `TZ="<zone>"`, then tab-separated date, time, offset, abbreviation and DST flag per transition (probe `zdump-i`)."##);
clause!(s31_10_g_4, "31.10", "Guarantees", r##"An abbreviation shorter than 3 characters gives `zdump: warning: zone "<zone>" abbreviation "<abbr>" has fewer than 3 characters` on standard error, exit 0 (probe `zdump-test`)."##);
clause!(s31_11_c_1, "31.11", "Contract", r##"Asks the user for a location and prints the time-zone value for it (tzselect(1))."##);
clause!(s31_11_i_1, "31.11", "Inputs", r##"`tzselect [--version] [--help] [-c COORD] [-n LIMIT]`: `-c` takes ISO 6709 coordinates and offers the nearest zones, `-n` the number offered (default 10) (probe `tzselect-help`)."##);
clause!(s31_11_i_2, "31.11", "Inputs", r##"Answers on standard input; the zone tables `zone1970.tab`, `zonenow.tab`, `iso3166.tab` of `/usr/share/zoneinfo` (tzselect(1))."##);
clause!(s31_11_g_1, "31.11", "Guarantees", r##"Prompts and menus on standard error, in order of distance with `-c` (probe `tzselect-eof`); the chosen value on standard output once confirmed (tzselect(1))."##);
clause!(s31_11_f_1, "31.11", "Failure", r##"End of input before the confirmation: exit 1 (probe `tzselect-eof`)."##);
clause!(s31_12_c_1, "31.12", "Contract", r##"Compiles message-catalog sources into the catalog format of Appendix D.2 that `catopen` reads (§7.8; POSIX `gencat`)."##);
clause!(s31_12_i_1, "31.12", "Inputs", r##"`gencat [OPTION...] -o OUTPUT-FILE [INPUT-FILE]...` or `gencat [OPTION...] [OUTPUT-FILE [INPUT-FILE]...]`; options `-H`/`--header=NAME`, `--new`, `-o`/`--output=NAME`, `-?`/`--help`, `--usage`, `-V`/`--version`; `-` is standard input or output (probe `gencat-help`)."##);
clause!(s31_12_g_1, "31.12", "Guarantees", r##"The catalog in the D.2 format (probe `gencat-compile`: a two-message source gives 72 bytes starting `de 08 04 96`; pending `UTIL-SPEC-3`); without `--new`, an existing catalog's messages are merged (POSIX `gencat`)."##);
clause!(s31_12_f_1, "31.12", "Failure", r##"An input that cannot be opened: ``cannot open input file `<file>': <strerror>``, exit 1 (probe `gencat-nofile`)."##);
clause!(s31_13_c_1, "31.13", "Contract", r##"Lists the shared objects loaded into a running process, those loaded with `dlopen` included (pldd(1))."##);
clause!(s31_13_i_1, "31.13", "Inputs", r##"`pldd [OPTION...] PID`; options `-?`/`--help`, `--usage`, `-V`/`--version` (probe `pldd-help`)."##);
clause!(s31_13_g_1, "31.13", "Guarantees", r##"A line with the process id and its program, then one line per loaded object (pldd(1)); the exact form is left to UTIL-15's probe, which needs a target the probe may trace."##);
clause!(s31_13_f_1, "31.13", "Failure", r##"No operand: `Exactly one parameter with process ID required.` and the `Try` line, exit 1 (probe `pldd-nopid`)."##);
clause!(s31_13_f_2, "31.13", "Failure", r##"No such process: `pldd: cannot open /proc/<pid>: No such file or directory`, exit 1 (probe `pldd-nosuchpid`)."##);
clause!(s31_13_f_3, "31.13", "Failure", r##"A process the caller may not trace: `pldd: cannot attach to process <pid>: Operation not permitted` (probe `pldd-self`)."##);
clause!(s31_14_c_1, "31.14", "Contract", r##"**Liella rule:** `iconvconfig` (the reference indexes its conversion modules; Liella has none, D-6.8), `/etc/bindresvport.blacklist` (Sun RPC is not implemented), and the `libc-devtools` commands `sprof`, `sotruss` and `mtrace` are not installed, and `nscd` is dropped (R8) (probe `iconvconfig-help`, `devtools`; pending `UTIL-SPEC-5`; differences row "Commands not installed")."##);
clause!(s31_14_c_2, "31.14", "Contract", r##"**Liella rule:** `locale-gen`, `update-locale` and `validlocale` of the `locales` package are Liella's own implementations from their man pages (locale-gen(8), update-locale(8)) and `/etc/locale.gen`, `/etc/default/locale` and `SUPPORTED` (pending `UTIL-SPEC-8`); their interface is specified with UTIL-13."##);
